WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.950
Here's what Learn leaves to
you, and what the kit adds.

2
00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:06.124
The log records every
write and its initiator,

3
00:00:06.124 --> 00:00:10.550
but not which identity may write
which value: that's the register.

4
00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:13.904
One enable activity covers
two lifecycle rows,

5
00:00:13.904 --> 00:00:17.688
hire and cancellation, which
must agree on one writer.

6
00:00:17.688 --> 00:00:22.901
Every change is logged, but testing each
successful protected write is yours.

7
00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:27.863
So are the saved queries, least privilege
per task, and evidence nobody edited.

8
00:00:27.863 --> 00:00:30.377
The verdict: use Learn's API as it is,

9
00:00:30.377 --> 00:00:33.840
and build the register
and the test against it.
